==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|confident|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkɑn.fɪ.dɑnt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a person in whom one can [[confide]] or share one's secrets: a friend
#* '''1675''', [[w:John Dryden|John Dryden]], ''Aureng-zebe'', William Miller (1808), page [https://books.google.com/books?id=KPoOAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA223&lpg=PA223&dq=you+love+me+for+no+other+end+than+to+become+my+confidant+and+friend+dryden&source=bl&ots=9C7--Vk9MH&sig=ijsttJA3UdsCaoh1PnEo3Q2I1H0&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwj04KfA99DJAhUE2GMKHZrHBEwQ6AEIMDAG#v=onepage&q&f=false 223]:
#*: Heaven made you love me for no other end, / But to become my '''confidant''' and friend: / As such, I keep no secret from your sight, […]

